From 84bf12a3d2f832ddae91e59e1e6f2548905d5ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 04:26:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 360 viewer: previous track, controller-driven quits, and two
 real exit bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One session arc, bundled like the bar-rework commit (0010) was - each piece
below is documented in its own section of docs/02-player-360.md in the
reverb-g2 repo, and the exit-deadlock investigation in docs/pruebas.jsonl
T105.

- Previous track: X on the left Touch controller (mirror of Y=next), 'p' on
  the keyboard. PreviousTrack() mirrors AdvanceTrack() with the wraparound
  inverted ((index + count - 1) % count - unsigned index, so count-1 instead
  of -1). Binding verified against real hardware; not yet exercised live
  going backward through a multi-file playlist.

- Background default flipped to black: HELLO_XR_THEME's default was
  "daylight" (medium grey), which for VR180 content paints the entire rear
  hemisphere grey - user wanted black ("hagamos negro todo por ahora").
  HELLO_XR_THEME=daylight opts back in. Confirmed live.

- Zoom/brightness no longer flash the progress bar: SetZoom()/
  SetBrightness() no longer call TouchInteraction() - they're image
  settings, not playback-position controls, and the auto-hide timer
  exists for the latter. Confirmed live.

- HELLO_XR_ANY_KEY_QUITS=1 (read once at startup): every control, keyboard
  or controller, also quits - except Menu, whose hold-to-confirm gesture is
  untouched. For the reverb-g2 repo's play-with-legend.sh controls-screen
  flow ("press anything to move on"). With it came the FIRST exit bug fix:
  PlayerControl's quit flag was only ever watched by the keyboard thread,
  which sits blocked in a read the whole time - a controller-driven quit set
  the flag and nothing noticed. PollActions() now latches
  xrRequestExitSession() when QuitRequested() goes true (latched - g_quit
  never clears, and calling xrRequestExitSession twice once the session has
  left RUNNING is a spec error).

- Exit bug two, the deep one - a guaranteed exit() deadlock on every
  controller-driven quit, latent since the Menu-quit patch (0005) and
  diagnosed with gdb on a live hang: the keyboard thread's getchar() holds
  stdin's stdio FILE lock for the whole blocking read, and glibc's exit()
  -> _IO_flush_all() needs that same lock. Any exit while that thread was
  still parked (i.e. every quit that came from the controller, since no
  key was ever pressed) deadlocked inside exit() with the XR session
  already ended - backlight on, process immortal. It was masked for days
  by two accidental backstops: interactive runs died to timeout's SIGTERM,
  and the old `sleep N |` stdin pipe delivered EOF at N seconds, waking
  the thread late. Fixed by reading keys via raw read(2) (ReadKeyByte()) -
  a kernel-level read holds no user-space locks, so the thread parks in it
  at exit() harmlessly. Bonus correctness: poll()+read() on the same fd is
  also more coherent than the old poll()+getchar() mix, where bytes could
  hide in stdio's buffer invisible to poll().

- Also from the same debugging: ~OpenXrProgram() destroyed the swapchain/
  session/instance with the last frame's GPU work potentially still in
  flight - the source of the vkFreeCommandBuffers/vkDestroySemaphore
  "in use" validation errors printed on every quit all along. New
  IGraphicsPlugin::WaitForGpuIdle() (default no-op; vkDeviceWaitIdle in
  the Vulkan backend), called first thing in the destructor.

Verified live with the headset on: controller button on the legend screen
-> legend closes -> next session starts immediately ("ahora funcionó, el
video arrancó al toque"). Keyboard paths re-verified via fake pty after the
raw-read switch: keys all work, clean exit in 0.06s.
